**Slide mix hint:** {{layoutSlideMixHint}}

The PPTX exporter reads layout from `brand/brand-pack.json` (`layoutStyle`: {{layoutStyle}}). Do not invent alternate visual systems in slide JSON — choose among the eight slide types and let the exporter apply {{layoutLabel}} framing.

## Slide Type Reference

1. **Title** — Primary or dark background, white text, deck title + subtitle (treatment varies by layout style)
2. **Agenda** — Light background, numbered items, title in Primary
3. **Section divider** — Primary or dark background, section number and title
4. **Content (single)** — White background, insight headline, bullets or narrative
5. **Two-column** — White background, side-by-side comparison
6. **Metrics** — White or light gray background, 2-4 large stat blocks in Primary
7. **Quote** — Light gray, white, or dark background, large pull quote, attribution
8. **Closing / Next steps** — Numbered action list, consistent with opening style
9. **Chart** — Native PPTX chart from JSON series (trends and comparisons)
10. **Diagram** — Process / architecture / swimlane from structured nodes (exporter draws shapes)
11. **Image** — Agent-generated illustration in `assets/` (prefer diagram/chart when possible)

## Footer logo

Every exported slide includes the {{customerName}} mark in the bottom-right corner (`brand/logo.png` on primary/dark slides, `brand/logo-on-light.png` on white/light slides).

## What Not to Do

- Do not use clip art, stock photo collages, or 3D effects
- Do not ask humans to drop PNGs into `assets/` — `visual-creator` generates image slides during `/build-deck`
- Do not invent precise chart numbers that are not in the brief
- Do not use more than 2 typefaces per slide
- Do not use WordArt or text shadows
- Do not include a slide title that is longer than one line
- Do not create slides that are purely decorative with no information
- Do not include your working notes or "draft" text in slides shared externally
- Do not ask the exporter for layouts outside {{layoutLabel}} — change layoutStyle in Studio and regenerate the zip instead
